  "notes": "West leads the ♥Q against 6♠. South wins the opening heart lead and must avoid losing tricks to the ♠Q and ♦Q. South has a two-way finesse in both spades and diamonds. South can guarantee his contract any time spades are 3-2 without taking any finesses.\n\nSouth should begin by cashing the ♠K and ♠A. When both opponents follow, South is home even if the ♠Q is still outstanding. South should cash dummy's other heart honour eliminating that suit.\n\nSouth now plays clubs. If the defender with the ♠Q ruffs at any point, he will be endplayed, forced to either pick up the ♦Q or concede a ruff and discard. If the defense allows South to cash all 4 rounds of clubs, South exits with a spade. The defender who wins the ♠Q will be similarily endplayed.\n\nIf spades prove to be 4-1, South should knock out he ♠Q and later play for the opponent short in spades to have the ♦Q.",
